s with a directory group\\u0027s members. User data alone lacks membership; group data alone lacks reporting peers.\u0022,\u0022odataQueries\u0022:[\u0022users?$filter=startswith(displayName,\\u0027{userName}\\u0027) or startswith(userPrincipalName,\\u0027{userName}\\u0027)\\u0026$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName and the group with\u0022,\u0022groups?$filter=startswith(displayName,\\u0027{groupName}\\u0027)\\u0026$select=id,displayName; clarify multiple matches\u0022,\u0022users(\\u0027{userId}\\u0027)/manager/directReports?$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName,jobTitle,department\u0022,\u0022groups(\\u0027{groupId}\\u0027)/members?$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName,jobTitle,department\u0022],\u0022toolBinding\u0022:\u0022list_users, get_users, get_users_manager, get_users_directReports, get_users_memberOf, get_users_drive, get_users_joinedTeams, get_users_chats, get_users_todoLists, list_groups, get_groups, get_groups_members, get_groups_owners, get_groups_drive, get_groups_team\u0022,\u0022toolBindings\u0022:[\u0022list_users\u0022,\u0022get_users\u0022,\u0022get_users_manager\u0022,\u0022get_users_directReports\u0022,\u0022get_users_memberOf\u0022,\u0022get_users_drive\u0022,\u0022get_users_joinedTeams\u0022,\u0022get_users_chats\u0022,\u0022get_users_todoLists\u0022,\u0022list_groups\u0022,\u0022get_groups\u0022,\u0022get_groups_members\u0022,\u0022get_groups_owners\u0022,\u0022get_groups_drive\u0022,\u0022get_groups_team\u0022],\u0022resourceBindings\u0022:[\u0022odata://Microsoft.Graph.GraphService/users\u0022,\u0022odata://Microsoft.Graph.GraphService/users/{key_id}\u0022,\u0022odata://Microsoft.Graph.GraphService/groups\u0022,\u0022odata://Microsoft.Graph.GraphService/groups/{key_id}\u0022],\u0022entitySets\u0022:[\u0022users\u0022,\u0022groups\u0022],\u0022template\u0022:\u0022Which peers of \\u0027{userName}\\u0027 belong to group \\u0027{groupName}\\u0027? 1. Resolve the user with GET users?$filter=startswith(displayName,\\u0027{userName}\\u0027) or startswith(userPrincipalName,\\u0027{userName}\\u0027)\\u0026$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName and the group with GET groups?$filter=startswith(displayName,\\u0027{groupName}\\u0027)\\u0026$select=id,displayName; clarify multiple matches. 2. Query GET users(\\u0027{userId}\\u0027)/manager/directReports?$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName,jobTitle,department and GET groups(\\u0027{groupId}\\u0027)/members?$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName,jobTitle,department. 3. Intersect the user\\u0027s reporting peers and group members by stable id or userPrincipalName, excluding the user. Both users and groups entity sets are required; do not infer directory membership from a shared manager. Report empty overlap and data provenance explicitly.\u0022,\u0022arguments\u0022:[{\u0022name\u0022:\u0022userName\u0022,\u0022description\u0022:\u0022User display name, ID, UPN, or me\u0022,\u0022required\u0022:false,\u0022default\u0022:\u0022Olga Podolyako\u0022},{\u0022name\u0022:\u0022groupName\u0022,\u0022description\u0022:\u0022Group display name or ID\u0022,\u0022required\u0022:false,\u0022default\u0022:\u0022Identity Architecture\u0022}]},{\u0022name\u0022:\u0022group_members_reporting_to_manager\u0022,\u0022title\u0022:\u0022Which group members report to a manager?\u0022,\u0022description\u0022:\u0022Filter group members by their reporting manager, joining group membership to user organization profiles.\u0022,\u0022odataQueries\u0022:[\u0022users?$filter=startswith(displayName,\\u0027{managerName}\\u0027) or startswith(userPrincipalName,\\u0027{managerName}\\u0027)\\u0026$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName and the group with\u0022,\u0022groups?$filter=startswith(displayName,\\u0027{groupName}\\u0027)\\u0026$select=id,displayName; clarify ambiguous identities\u0022,\u0022groups(\\u0027{groupId}\\u0027)/members?$select=id,displayName,userPrincipalName,jobTitle,department to enumerate members\u0022,\u0022users(\\u0027{managerId}\\u0027)/directReports?$